INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'_rank_math_title','دليل تقني لقياس وتثبيت أنبوب حلزوني 160 ملم للمزارع' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='_rank_math_title');
INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'_rank_math_description','دليل شامل للمزارعين لقياس وتثبيت أنبوب حلزوني 160 ملم، يغطي الحسابات التقنية والنقاط التنفيذية خطوة بخطوة.' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='_rank_math_description');
INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'rank_math_focus_keyword','دليل شامل لقياس وتثبيت أنبوب حلزوني 160 ملم للمزارع: من الحسابات التقنية إلى النقاط التنفيذية' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='rank_math_focus_keyword');
INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: The Importance of Precise Pipe Sizing in Farms</h2><p>In the design of drip and trickle irrigation systems, one of the most complex yet critical steps is selecting the appropriate size for the main line. Thin-walled plastic pipes with threaded connections have become a popular alternative to older metal pipes due to their flexibility and high chemical resistance. The size <strong>160 millimeters</strong> is one of the most commonly used dimensions in medium-to-large farms, as it strikes a good balance between water flow and fluid velocity while appearing logical in terms of installation and maintenance costs.</p><p>Many farmers decide on the purchase of these pipes based on guesswork; however, precise hydraulic calculations are necessary to prevent excessive pressure drop at the end of the line and unutilized water. This article aims to introduce you to the logic of selecting a 160 mm pipe by explaining the demand-based conditional process in irrigation.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Technical principles for measuring and calculating the diameter of a 160 mm pipe</h2><h3>The relationship between total farm flow rate and pipe diameter</h3><p>160 millimeter threaded pipes are generally designed to handle flow rates in the range of 60 to 150 liters per minute. If the output flow rate from your well or reservoir is lower than this range, using a 160 mm pipe may reduce the fluid velocity below the critical limit (approximately 1 meter per second), leading to sedimentation at the bottom of the pipe. Conversely, if the flow rate is significantly higher, fluid velocity will increase, and pipe friction will cause a severe pressure drop.</p><p>To perform the calculation, you must first aggregate the total flow rate required for your drip irrigation network. For example, if your system includes 20 laterals with a flow rate of 5 liters per minute each, the total flow rate is 100 liters per minute. This flow rate makes the 160 mm pipe an ideal option, as it maintains the flow velocity within the safe range (1.5 to 2.5 meters per second). Accurate flow rate calculation sometimes requires considering factors such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%D8%B3%D9%88%DB%8C%D8%A7-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">seed quantity per hectare</a> and plant transpiration intensity to determine the precise water requirement.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/اندازهگیری-لوله-نخدار-160-میلیمتر-برای-مزرعه-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="اندازه‌گیری لوله نخدار 160 میلیمتر برای مزرعه - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>product sizing farm irrigation 160 mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure><h3>friction factor and pressure loss along the pipe</h3><p>PVC and PE pipes have different friction factors compared to steel or cast iron. In technical calculations, the Darcy-Weisbach formula is used. For a 160 mm pipe, the pressure loss per 100 meters of pipe depends directly on the flow rate. For example, at a flow rate of 100 liters per minute, the pressure loss in a 160 mm pipe is approximately 0.5 to 0.8 meters of water column. If the length of your main pipe exceeds 200 meters, you need to perform a more precise pressure loss calculation to ensure that the pressure at the end of the line is sufficient to operate sprinklers or drip lines.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Practical tips for installing and connecting 160 mm threaded pipe</h2><h3>Correct threaded connection technique (Crimp vs. Threaded)</h3><p>A key advantage of 160 mm pipes for small to medium-sized farms is the ability to use threaded connections. However, note that threaded connections are only suitable for metal-to-plastic joints or screw-type fittings. For plastic-to-plastic pipe joints, always use metal or plastic couplings with crimp caps. Over-tightening threaded fittings on 160 mm pipes can cause the pipe wall to crack due to internal pressure and cold-snap effects. Use Teflon tape or aquarium cement at threaded joints to prevent leaks, but never apply mechanical force directly to the pipe body.</p><h3>Pressure management on farm slopes</h3><p>The greatest challenge for 160 mm pipes is pressure variation caused by steep slopes. If your farm has a slope, the 160 mm pipe at the low-lying area will face higher pressure than the upslope section. This can cause joint failures or water leaks at downstream points. The solution is to install pressure regulating valves (PRV) at the beginning of the main lines. To optimize the system, it is essential to understand the function of irrigation drip tape and how it performs under variable pressures to prevent water loss in high-pressure zones.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/اندازهگیری-لوله-نخدار-160-میلیمتر-برای-مزرعه-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="اندازه‌گیری لوله نخدار 160 میلیمتر برای مزرعه - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>product sizing farm irrigation 160 millimeter threaded pipe</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Functional comparison with separate sizes</h2><table><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>125 millimeter pipe</th><th>160 millimeter pipe</th><th>200 mm pipe</th></tr><tr><td>Recommended flow rate (L/min)</td><td>40 to 80</td><td>60 to 120</td><td>120 to 200</th></tr><tr><td>Pressure drop (per 100 m - at average flow rate)</td><td>Low</td><td>Medium</td><td>Very low</td></tr><tr><td>Relative cost</td><td>1</td><td>1.5</td><td>2.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ideal application</td><td>Small farms / secondary lines</td><td>Medium farms / main line</td><td>Large Farms/Main Line</td></tr></table><p>As shown in the table, a 160 mm pipe provides the balance point. Selecting a 200 mm pipe is more expensive and is only justified for farms that require a flow rate exceeding 120 liters per minute without significant pressure drop. However, for most farms in Iran, a 160 mm pipe with a standard pumping system is the more cost-effective option.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2><h3>Is 160 mm threaded pipe resistant to sunlight?</h3><p>Yes, polyethylene (PE) and polyvinyl chloride (PVC) pipes contain UV stabilizers. However, continuous and direct exposure to intense sunlight can cause discoloration and increased brittleness of the pipe walls over time. It is recommended to install the main pipe in shallow channels or underground, or to use protective covers.</p><h3>What is the maximum allowable operating pressure for a 160 mm pipe?</h3><p>The standard operating pressure for a 160 mm pipe is typically between 5 and 8 bar, depending on wall thickness and manufacturing quality. If your well pressure exceeds 8 bar, you must use a main pressure regulator, as pressures above 10 bar can weaken fittings and cause leaks at 160 mm pipe connections.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/اندازهگیری-لوله-نخدار-160-میلیمتر-برای-مزرعه-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="اندازه‌گیری لوله نخدار 160 میلیمتر برای مزرعه - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>product sizing farm irrigation 160 mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure><h3>How can I tell if the pipe is properly adjusted?</h3><p>After installation, run the system at full flow rate. Use a reliable manometer or pressure gauge to measure pressure at the line inlet and outlet (last dripper). If pressure drop exceeds 10 to 15 percent, you should check whether the pipe diameter is too small or the slope is too steep. Also, studying the carrot seed rate per hectare and its irrigation requirements can help you determine a more precise flow rate for network design.</p>\n\n<h2>Summary and Final Recommendations</h2><p>Using a 160 mm threaded pipe is one of the smartest decisions in farm irrigation network design, provided that the measurement and installation processes are performed with engineering precision. This size offers high flexibility for farms ranging from 1 to 15 hectares. The key to success is matching the output flow rate of the pump or well with the pipe diameter and considering field slopes. By following the principles outlined in this guide and using high-quality fittings, you can prevent unauthorized pressure drops, hidden leaks, and costly repair expenses. Always remember that a good irrigation system is the main foundation for increasing the yield of barley per hectare and other crops. With proper water management, you not only reduce costs but also ensure product quality.</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D8%B4%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%B7-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AA%D9%86%D9%82%D9%8A%D8%B7-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%B3%DB%8C%D9%87/">D8B4D8B1D98AD8B7 D8A7D984D8B1D98A D8A8D8A7D984D8AAD986D982D98AD8B7 D981D98A D982D8A7D8AFD8B3DB8CD987</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/clover-seed-per-hectare-guide-farmers/">clover seed per hectare guide farmers</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/yield-of-dryland-barley-per-hectare-tips-increase-production/">yield of dryland barley per hectare tips increase production</a></p>','Comprehensive Guide to Measuring and Installing 160 mm Ribbed Pipes for Farms: From Technical Calculations to Execution','Correct selection and sizing of main lines, particularly the 160 mm model, determine the long-term costs and yield of irrigation systems. In this technical guide, you will learn about hydraulic principles, threaded connection methods, and strategies for reducing pressure loss in large-scale farms.','publish','closed','closed','160mm-ribbed-pipe-installation-guide-farms',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
